Z||000000||glava2876||05-26-2001||08:24 PM||||I finally have fuel and I had the Iron Duke running today. Now on to the next item -the exhaust. My car has low original miles and still has the original totally welded exhaust.When I had the engine running, it wouldn't idle and ran a little rough and sounded funny. When I went behind the car I saw some insulation on the floor-most likely part of a mouse house. I don't think it all came out. Is there a way to get the rest out? Also, the bottom part of the outer shell of the cat. fell off. The inner stell shell is fully intact. Has anyone ever fabricated a new cover for this problem? I thought I could fabricate an upper and lower cover out of aluminum -with a 1/2" lip on each. I though I could then wrap the steel shell with header wrap or other insulation and install the aluminim cover over it -riveting at the lip. Anyone think this is possible or have another method? I hate to trash a good exhaust system just because of these problems. Thanks, Glen||||reg||12
Z||000001||PBJ||05-26-2001||09:58 PM||||About the mouse house-it will clear itself out.  The converter heat shield, again I would not be concerned about replacing it either. I have put new converters on 3 of my fiero's so far and they do not even come with a shield on them.  This shield is more for extended idle over flamable ground, ie. dry grass.  If I where to fabricate a heat shield I would attach it to the sub-frame or body rather than the exhaust that would shake this shield loose.||||reg||1
